## Infrastructure Issues & Limitations

1. SSL Termination at the Load Balancer

SSL termination at the load balancer means that the load balancer decrypts HTTPS traffic.

The traffic between the load balancer and the web servers may then be unencrypted if HTTPS is not configured internally.

This can be a security issue because sensitive data may be exposed inside the network.

2. Only One MySQL Server Can Accept Writes

Only the MySQL Primary server can accept write operations.

This creates a bottleneck because all writes must go through one database server.

If the Primary database fails, the application cannot perform write operations until the Primary is restored or a Replica is promoted.

3. Servers Contain All Components

Having the web server, application server, and database components together on the same servers can cause several problems.

These include:

* Poor separation of responsibilities
* Resource competition between components
* Difficulty scaling components independently
* A database-heavy workload affecting web and application performance
* More complicated maintenance and troubleshooting
* A security issue on one component potentially affecting other components on the same server
